 {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le14ob04re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "One syllable words with silent -e"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " "}, {"type": "text", "content": "There are 5 spelling rules for the silent e."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Rules\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"1. A final e makes the vowel say its name.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">cut</br>cute</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"2. English words don't end in v or u.</p> The e after v or u does not affect pronunciation.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">have</br>blue</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"3. Silent e after the letter c and g \u201csoften\u201d their sounds.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">rage</br>cabbage</br>face</br>experience</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"4. Every syllable must have a vowel. The final syllable can be pronounced without a vowel but every syllable must have a vowel.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">tackle</br>pickle</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"5. Sometimes the silent final e has no purpose.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">are</br>were</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Weak Forms"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Weak forms happen on small, less important words that link the operative, key <span class=\"strong\">content words</span> of a sentence together. "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Less Important Words\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Example</span> am, are, be, been, can, could, do, does, has, was</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Prepositions\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">at, for, from, of, to</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Pronouns\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">he, her, him, his, me, she, them, us, we, you, your</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Verbs\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">am, is, was\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Conjunctions\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">and, but, or, than, that</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Articles\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">a, the, an</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "stuffed animal"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a toy in the shape of an animal that usually has fake fur and is filled with soft material"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I love my old stuffed animals."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le14ob04aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you talk about a room in a house."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "closet"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a small room that is used for storing things"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There are a lot of old clothes in my closet."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le14ob04aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "poster"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a large picture that is put on walls as a decoration"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I kept your toys and posters."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le14ob04aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "memento"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something that is kept as a reminder of a person, place, or thing"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'll take Pugsly back to my apartment as a little momento."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le14ob04aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "comforter"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a thick bed covering that is filled with a soft light material"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:You even kept my old unicorn comforter with the rainbows."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le14ob04aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "goth"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who listens to or performs goth music, wears mostly black clothing, uses black and white makeup, and often has dyed black hair"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I was in my goth phase."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le14ob04aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "phase"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a short period of time during which a person behaves in a particular way or likes a particular thing"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: That was a challenging phase in my life."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le14ob04aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "unicorn"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an imaginary animal that looks like a horse and has a straight horn growing from the middle of its forehead"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I have a unicorn comforter from my childhood."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le14ob04aud08"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Make a list of 10 objects you have from your childhood."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Choose 5 things and write a sentence for each."}, {"type": "text", "content": "With a partner, explain why you still have these items.  Why are they important to you?"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I make a list of important items from my past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write 5 sentences about these items."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I explain why I still have them to a partner."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn5le14ob04re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn5le14ob04re2img06.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn5le14ob04re2img06.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally's Mom</span>: You must be happy to be back after such a long flight.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Yes, my bedroom brings back so many memories! Oh my old stuffed animals. I still love them.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally's Mom</span>: There are at least five more in the closet.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Pugsly, my stuffed dog. He's so cute.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally's Mom</span>: Yes, I kept your toys and posters.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn5le14ob04re2img06.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Oh Mom, that's sweet. You even kept my old unicorn comforter with the rainbows!</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally's Mom</span>: Honey, I'll never throw anything of yours out.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Nothing?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally's Mom</span>: Well, there were some old clothes from your teenage years.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Oh my goth phase ... the black clothes and lipstick.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally's Mom</span>: Don't you love all the old photographs of your friends too?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Yes, and look at this note I wrote to my penpal in South Africa.", "id": 2, "time": "21500", "image": "engenn5le14ob04re2img07.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally's Mom</span>: What was her name again?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Rita de Boer.  She used to send me little presents too!</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally's Mom</span>: What are you doing?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Could I take Pugsly back with me to my apartment as a little memento?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally's Mom</span>: Sure. I hope that cat of yours, Meenee, doesn't get too upset.", "id": 3, "time": "48300", "image": "engenn5le14ob04re2img08.jpg"}]}}]}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instruc